---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
// This URL exists on the legacy site (/services) and is the only one search engines currently index for the
// domain, so it is kept rather than redirected. Describes what the service does — no prices, no guarantees.
// Only what this service does today is stated here; nothing planned or unavailable is described (owner decision 2026-10-24).
---
<Base title="Our services" description="What we do today for applicants to Ukrainian medical universities: a free enquiry, guidance, and university facts shown only once officially checked.">
  <div class="page-head"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Services</span><h1>What we do for applicants</h1><p>Independent help for international students applying to medical universities in Ukraine. Below: what we do for you today, what we never promise, and what it costs.</p></div></div>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Services' }]} />
  <section style="padding-top:1rem"><div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="today">What we do today (free)</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="card"><div class="ico" aria-hidden="true">1</div><h3>Answers by email</h3><p>Tell us your course, preferred universities and background in a short online profile. We read it and reply by email with answers to your questions and the next steps we suggest. Where a university's requirements have not yet been verified from its official pages, we say so.</p><a class="more" href="/apply/">Start your profile →</a></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="ico" aria-hidden="true">2</div><h3>Document questions</h3><p>The Apply Online form lets you mark each document as have, need or not sure. We answer document questions by email, including on translations, notarisation and legalisation.</p><a class="more" href="/admissions/#documents">Document guidance →</a></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="ico" aria-hidden="true">3</div><h3>Choosing a university and course</h3><p>We help you work out what to compare: whether your course is open to applicants from your country this intake, the language of instruction, the qualification title, the published fee and the entry requirements. Each fact appears on a university's profile once it has been verified.</p><a class="more" href="/universities/">See the universities we are researching →</a></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="ico" aria-hidden="true">4</div><h3>What comes next</h3><p>We explain by email what comes next at each stage, including the invitation letter and visa steps that the university and the authorities control.</p><a class="more" href="/admissions/#stages">The four stages →</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <h2 id="limits">What we never promise</h2>
      <p>Admission, a visa, recognition of a qualification in any country, scholarships or employment. Admission decisions are made solely by the university, visa decisions by the relevant authorities, and recognition by the regulator in the country where you plan to work. See our <a href="/disclosure/">independence and referral disclosure</a>.</p>
      <h2 id="cost">What it costs</h2>
      <p>No paid service is offered at present, and starting an application is free. If a paid service is introduced, every option will be described in full before you choose it: inclusions, exclusions, price, when payment is due and the refund terms. Any fee of ours will always be shown separately from university fees, which are paid to the university.</p>
      <p>Questions first? See the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> or <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <CtaBand title="Start with a free enquiry" text="Tell us your course and your questions. We reply by email, and nothing is sent to a university until you confirm." whatsapp="Our services" />
</Base>
